=== ir_control.rs 575-615 (the deopt-after-side-effect dataflow) ===
575:/// effect is executed on SOME path reaching `i`. The join is UNION (may-reach):
576:/// a merge is tainted if ANY incoming edge carries an effect — a must-join would
577:/// silently admit the diamond hazard (one effect-free arm "washing" the merge).
578:/// A runtime-deopt-capable instruction is rejected iff an effect can reach it.
579:/// Rejection is the normal `mark_unsupported` / interpreter fallback — no new
580:/// channel. Authorities reused unchanged in role: `is_observable_side_effect`
581:/// (what taints) and `is_runtime_deopt_capable` (what is guarded).
582:fn reject_deopt_after_side_effect(
583:    instructions: &[Instruction],
584:    labels: &HashMap<u32, usize>,
585:) -> Result<(), JitError> {
586:    let len = instructions.len();
587:    let successors: Vec<Vec<usize>> = (0..len)
588:        .map(|index| control_flow_successors(index, instructions, labels))
589:        .collect();
590:
591:    // Forward union dataflow to fixpoint: seed every node, propagate an effect to
592:    // successors, re-enqueue on any false->true flip (monotone, so it terminates).
593:    let mut effect_in = vec![false; len];
594:    let mut worklist: Vec<usize> = (0..len).collect();
595:    while let Some(index) = worklist.pop() {
596:        let effect_out = effect_in[index] || is_observable_side_effect(&instructions[index]);
597:        if effect_out {
598:            for &successor in &successors[index] {
599:                if !effect_in[successor] {
600:                    effect_in[successor] = true;
601:                    worklist.push(successor);
602:                }
603:            }
604:        }
605:    }
606:
607:    for (index, instruction) in instructions.iter().enumerate() {
608:        if effect_in[index] && is_runtime_deopt_capable(instruction) {
609:            return Err(JitError::UnsupportedOpcode {
610:                opcode: format!(
611:                    "runtime-deopt-capable {} is reachable after an observable side effect \
612:                     (a deopt would replay the effect on restart)",
613:                    opcode_name(instruction)
614:                ),
615:            });

